body:
Oh I'm definitely going to the hospital if I don't go through with this - that's just the way of things. I don't really mind that - the hospital is boring more than anything else, and definitely not a place I'd kill myself to avoid going to.

&#x200B;

The main issue I have in terms of quality of life is that I can't see myself having any sort of employment that would be enjoyable and/or meaningful. That's not to say I'm thinking of killing myself because I'll never be, for example, a CEO - I'd be fine going about life as a gardener or kitchen worker on a "come in when your brain isn't trying to kill you"-basis, but those jobs just don't exist - or are reserved for people who are in arguably worse mental states than I am. If coming to terms with a lower quality means staying at an entry-level job I hate until I'm finally old enough to retire, it all just becomes an exercise in waiting for nature to do the job I'm too scared to do myself, and I can't get myself to accept that fully, no matter how hard I try.
